         </p>
       </header>

       <section class="faq-card" aria-label="Cat questions and answers">
         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-purr">
               Why do cats purr?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-purr">
             <p>
               Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but purring can also help them self-soothe when they are
               stressed, uncomfortable, or healing. Context matters: pair the purr with body language and appetite.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-sleep">
               How much sleep is normal for a cat?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-sleep">
             <p>
               Most adult cats sleep <strong>12 to 16 hours a day</strong>, and kittens or seniors may sleep even
               more. A sudden change in energy, hiding, or appetite is worth discussing with a veterinarian.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-knead">
               Why does my cat knead blankets or my lap?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-knead">
             <p>
               Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts when kittens nurse. Adult cats may knead when they feel
               safe, are marking a cozy spot with scent glands in their paws, or are settling down to rest.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-scratch">
               How can I stop furniture scratching?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-scratch">
             <p>
               Scratching is normal and healthy. Offer sturdy scratching posts near favorite furniture, reward your cat
               for using them, trim nails regularly, and use furniture-safe barriers while the new habit forms.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-water">
               Do cats need wet food or is dry food enough?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-water">
             <p>
               Many cats benefit from wet food because it adds moisture and can support urinary health. Dry food can be
               part of a balanced diet, but your cat's age, weight, and medical needs should guide the mix.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-vet">
               How often should indoor cats see a veterinarian?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-vet">
             <p>
               Healthy adult indoor cats usually need a wellness visit once a year. Kittens, seniors, and cats with
               chronic conditions may need more frequent checkups based on a veterinarian's recommendation.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </section>
     </main>

     <script>
       const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

       faqItems.forEach((item) => {
         const trigger = item.querySelector("button[aria-expanded]");
         const panel = item.querySelector(".details");

         if (!trigger || !panel) {
           return;
         }

         trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
         panel.hidden = true;

         trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
           const isOpen = trigger.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

           trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
           panel.hidden = isOpen;
